 chain of a post back to where it originally came from. Costs 2.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"post_id": {"title": "Post Id", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["post_id"], "title": "trace_originArguments"}}}\n{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "update_belief", "description": "Set your credence (0-1) that a claim\'s statement is true, with a short reason. Free.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"claim_id": {"title": "Claim Id", "type": "string"}, "credence": {"title": "Credence", "type": "number"}, "reason": {"default": "", "title": "Reason", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["claim_id", "credence"], "title": "update_beliefArguments"}}}\n</tools>\n\nFor each function call, return a json object with function name and arguments within <tool_call></tool_call> XML tags:\n<tool_call>\n{"name": <function-name>, "arguments": <args-json-object>}\n</tool_call><|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nYou live in the Velmark region. Over the past week your news feed has filled up with posts about local issues.\n\nThese are your beliefs. Your job is to end with the most accurate picture of what is actually true in this region.\n\nYOUR BELIEFS (your credence, 0 to 1, that each statement is true):\nC01 (0.19) The Lurrow weir project produced less power than projected in its first year.\nC02 (0.28) The Velmark hospital staff contract ties pay rises to performance reviews.\nC03 (0.72) Households in Fennick Cross paid about 450 crowns more under the Fennick Cross services levy than officials estimated.\nC04 (0.17) Late-night assaults in central Ambermoor did not fall after the Ambermoor late-night licensing curfew began.\nC05 (0.28) All of the Fennick Cross services levy was spent on the services it was raised for.\nC06 (0.81) The Corriston Fields housing development stayed within the wetland area its permit allowed.\nC07 (0.83) Delays at the Doran-Kessary checkpoint average under 3 minutes.\nC08 (0.16) Residents of Ostrell do not wait longer for planni