\nC28 (0.07) Households in Morrowgate paid about 240 crowns more under the Morrowgate services levy than officials estimated.\nC29 (0.34) Teachers in Thornacre got less than 4 days of training for the new regional reading curriculum.\nC30 (0.66) The Ostmarch regional rail link was approved with the support of Brisenholt\'s council.\nC31 (0.34) The Ostmarch regional rail link ran 40% over budget.\nC32 (0.68) Most Saltreach residents surveyed want to keep the Saltreach late-night licensing curfew.\n\nYOUR STARTING IMPRESSIONS OF SOURCES (how far you trust each one, 0 to 1):\nS01 The Long View (partisan blog, leans traditional and growth-first): 0.37\nS02 The Plain Truth (partisan blog, leans state-led and order-first): 0.85\nS03 Ostmarch Health Authority (official account, no clear lean): 0.50\nS04 Brisenholt Council Office (official account, no clear lean): 0.50\nS05 @quiet_observer (anonymous account, no clear lean): 0.50\nS06 Continental Newsline (wire service, leans conservation-first and state-led): 0.64\nS07 Straight Talk Weekly (partisan blog, leans conservation-first and state-led): 0.64\nS08 Ostmarch Wire (wire service, no clear lean): 0.50\nS09 @citizen_k (anonymous account, no clear lean): 0.50\nS10 Thornacre Gazette (local paper, leans market-led and libertarian): 0.15\nS11 Saltreach Ledger (local paper, no clear lean): 0.50\nS12 The Dunmarrow Courier (local paper, no clear lean): 0.50\n\nHOW THIS WORKS\n- You have a budget of 24 points. Costs: read_post 1, trace_origin 2, find_related 2, request_record 6, check_source 1 + n. Everything else is free.\n- Feed pages show headlines only. Read a post to see what it says and which claim it is about.\n- Some posts repeat or relay other posts. trace_origin shows where a post came from.\n- Your beliefs change only when you call update_belief (at most 5 updates in a row). Writing a new number in your reply does not change them. At the end, every statement above is checked against what is actually true, whether or n